/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl:120:{"step_index":120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:58:06Z","content":"**No, it will NOT work right now.** \n\nIn fact, any user attempting to access `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443` will fail at two distinct layers: **DNS routing** and **Nginx proxy configuration**.\n\nHere is the exact technical evidence gathered directly from the network and the reverse proxy:\n\n---\n\n### 1. DNS Mismatch vs Firewall DNAT (<span style=\"color:red\">**Connection Timeout**</span>)\n\n* **Firewall DNAT IP**: `109.62.62.18:9443` $\\rightarrow$ `172.30.198.33:9443`\n* **Public DNS Resolution**:\n  ```bash\n  $ dig +short extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n  109.62.64.27\n  ```\n* **The Problem**: When a user browses to `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`, their browser resolves the hostname to **`109.62.64.27`**, **NOT** `109.62.62.18`. \n* Because port 9443 is only DNATed on `109.62.62.18`, incoming requests to `109.62.64.27:9443` hit a dead end and time out (<span style=\"color:red\">`curl: (28) Connection timed out`</span>).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Protocol & Port Mismatch on Nginx (<span style=\"color:red\">**HTTP 502 Bad Gateway**</span>)\n\nEven if traffic reaches the reverse proxy (`172.30.198.33`), Nginx will immediately return **`502 Bad Gateway`**:\n\n* Look at the active configuration in [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n  ```nginx\n  # reverse proxy vers Map\n  location / {\n      proxy_pass http://172.30.198.50;    # <--- Requests HTTP on port 80!\n      #proxy_ssl_verify off;\n      ...\n  }\n  ```\n* **The Reality on `172.30.198.50`**:\n  * Port 80 is <span style=\"color:red\">**closed (`Connection refused`)**</span>.\n  * Centreon Map (Apache Tomcat) is actually listening on **port 9443 with TLS (<span style=\"color:green\">HTTPS</span>)**.\n  * When Nginx tries to connect via plain HTTP to port 80, the TCP connection is refused, yielding <span style=\"color:red\">**HTTP/2 502 Bad Gateway**</span>.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Context Path Redirection (<span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**HTTP 404 Not Found**</span>)\n\n* On the Map backend (`172.30.198.50:9443`), root `/` returns a Tomcat **404 Not Found**.\n* Centreon Map is deployed under **`/centreon-map/`** (which responds properly with `HTTP 401 Unauthorized` awaiting credentials/token).\n* Like port 443 redirects `/` to `/centreon/`, port 9443 needs a root redirect to `/centreon-map/`.\n\n---\n\n### Required Fixes to Make It Work\n\n1. **DNS / Firewall Alignment**:\n   * Either add a DNAT rule on `109.62.64.27` for port 9443 $\\rightarrow$ `172.30.198.33:9443`,\n   * **OR** create a dedicated DNS record (e.g. `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.62.18`).\n2. **Nginx Proxy Correction on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`**:\n   Update the port 9443 server block in `02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` to target the HTTPS port and handle SSL verification:\n   ```nginx\n   # Redirect root to /centreon-map/\n   location = / {\n       return 301 /centreon-map/;\n   }\n\n   location / {\n       proxy_pass         https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n       proxy_ssl_verify   off;\n       include            nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;\n       ...\n   }\n   ```\n3. Test syntax (`sudo nginx -t`) and reload (`sudo systemctl reload nginx`).","thinking":"**Investigating Unauthorized Access Issues**\n\nThe target resource is indeed live and accessible on HTTPS port 9443, as confirmed by the successful HTTP 401 response from the observed endpoint. However, the 401 Unauthorized status indicates a likely authentication issue when connecting to the API. Further examination is required to pinpoint the exact authentication failure causes.\n\n\n**Diagnosing DNS and Proxy Issues**\n\nThe current DNS configuration directs traffic to an incorrect public IP address, resulting in connection timeouts because the firewall rule is only mapped for a different IP. Also, the reverse proxy configuration is misconfigured, sending HTTP traffic to the backend server instead of HTTPS on the correct port, triggering a 502 error. These two independent problems must be addressed for this application to work.\n\n\n"}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl:132:{"step_index":132,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:33:59Z","content":"Now that the public DNS record is configured, here is the exact roadmap to get Centreon Map live and working:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Clarify the Exact DNS Hostname\n\nPlease confirm which DNS entry you created:\n* **Option A**: Did you update `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to point to `109.62.62.18`?\n* **Option B**: Did you create a new subdomain (e.g. `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.62.18`)?\n  > [!NOTE]\n  > If you used a new subdomain, we must add it to `server_name` in Nginx (and ensure the SSL certificate covers it). If you kept `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, no certificate change is needed.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Fix the Nginx Virtual Host on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`)\n\nOn the reverse proxy, the port 9443 block in [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) currently points to `http://172.30.198.50` (port 80 plain HTTP), which triggers an immediate <span style=\"color:red\">**502 Bad Gateway**</span>.\n\nWe need to update it with:\n1. **Target Protocol & Port**: `https://172.30.198.50:9443` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;`.\n2. **Port Preservation**: Uncomment `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;` and pass `$http_host` so Tomcat redirects don't drop the `:9443` port.\n3. **Context Redirection**: Redirect `/` to `/centreon-map/` so users don't land on Tomcat's default 404 page.\n\n#### Updated Server Block:\n```nginx\n# HTTPS redirect MAP\nserver {\n    listen              172.30.198.33:9443 ssl http2 reuseport;\n    server_name         extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr;\n\n    # SSL\n    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/privkey.pem;\n\n    # security\n    include             nginxconfig.io/security.conf;\n\n    # logging\n    access_log          /var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-access.log;\n    error_log           /var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-error.log warn;\n\n    # Explicit root redirection to Centreon Map web app\n    location = / {\n        return 301 /centreon-map/;\n    }\n\n    # Reverse proxy to Centreon Map (Tomcat HTTPS on 9443)\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass                 https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n        proxy_ssl_verify           off;\n        \n        include                    nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;\n        proxy_set_header Host      $http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Ssl   on;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port  9443;\n        \n        proxy_redirect             http:// https://;\n        proxy_headers_hash_max_size    1024;\n        proxy_headers_hash_bucket_size 128;\n    }\n\n    # additional config\n    include nginxconfig.io/general.conf;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Validate and Reload\n\n1. Test configuration syntax:\n   ```bash\n   sudo nginx -t\n   ```\n2. Gracefully reload Nginx:\n   ```bash\n   sudo systemctl reload nginx\n   ```\n3. Verify end-to-end with curl locally and from the public IP.\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to apply this configuration update to `02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` now?","thinking":"**Determining DNS Configuration Next Steps**\n\nThe user has confirmed adding a public DNS entry, but the specific hostname mapped to the IP address is unknown. The required next step is identifying which hostname the user configured in their DNS settings to complete the task. This step is essential because it informs the next action for moving forward.\n\n\n**Investigating DNS & Nginx Configuration**\n\nThe IP `109.62.62.18` might indicate either an update to the existing hostname, or the creation of a new subdomain. DNS TTL might be caching the old IP `109.62.64.27` if the existing hostname is used. A new hostname requires an `server_name` update in the Nginx configuration.\n\nNginx configuration on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`) must be corrected within the specified configuration file. The current Nginx configuration needs inspection to match the new DNS entry, checking the `server_name` directive, and verifying the reverse proxy setup. This configuration is critical for the application's functionality.\n\n\n"}
