tremer-telecom.fr\n     ```\n     *(Or via DNS-01 challenge using `~/.ansible/playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml`).*\n2. **Reload Nginx**:\n   * Once renewed, run `sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx`.\n3. **Retest UI Button**:\n   * Re-run `[Test connection to server]` in Centreon Web (`Administration > Extensions > Options`). With a matching SAN in the certificate, PHP cURL will validate the TLS handshake and show a green success mark.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n* All background tasks have been terminated (`manage_task` kill); no lingering background processes exist.\n* Strict caution: avoid running intrusive background tests or modifying unrelated firewall rules without explicit user request.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 1 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.agents/agents/koby-bowser-nginx/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-10T07:28:04Z"}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000006.jsonl:2:{"step_index":438,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:52:46Z","thinking":"**Summarizing Findings and Configurations**\n\nFindings are being compiled, encompassing identified issues and applied configurations. The summary will explain the rationale behind each configuration change. The chain's current operational status will be included in the summary.\n\n\n**Creating Comprehensive Report Artifact**\n\nThe request calls for a detailed report, including findings, configurations, and status. An artifact will be generated, as it aligns with instructions for comprehensive summaries. This artifact will comprehensively address the user's specific request. The artifact directory is being accessed to manage the file creation.\n\n\n**Analyzing Certificate Verification Failure**\n\nThe initial investigation confirmed network connectivity and the presence of a TLS-enabled Tomcat server. Strict TLS verification within the web application is likely failing because the expected certificate is not trusted.  Bypassing TLS verification in CLI tests succeeds, confirming underlying connectivity. The mismatch in trust is the central focus now.\n\n\n**Diagnosing Certificate Validation Failure**\n\nThe identified root cause is a Subject Alternative Name (SAN) mismatch during TLS verification. The certificate issued for the Nginx reverse proxy `th2-revproxyp-fe1` lacks `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`. This results in SSL verification failures when PHP cURL attempts to connect.\n\n**Applying Reverse Proxy Configuration**\n\nThe Nginx configuration was updated to address the SAN mismatch by explicitly including `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` and `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` within the `server_name` directive. `proxy_ssl_verify off;` was used temporarily due to the self-signed certificate, with `proxy_pass` set to the correct backend and port. HTTP headers were set to preserve the correct port and protocol for the backend service.\n\n\n**Configuring Loopback Alias and Host Resolution**\n\nA loopback alias was configured to accept local packets addressed to a public IP, avoiding external routing. The `/etc/hosts` file on the backend was updated to resolve the public FQDN directly to the reverse proxy's internal DMZ IP, bypassing firewall NAT limitations.\n\n**Assessing Chain's Operational Status**\n\nThe system data flow was examined, highlighting how external browsers access the map service. The central backend PHP path was verified, confirming network and proxy functionality. The reverse proxy and backend host resolution are active.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive architecture and status report for Centreon Map integration via reverse proxy th2-revproxyp-fe1 and Central th2-centprop-be1. Details findings (502 root cause, hairpin NAT limitations, SSL SAN validation failure), all applied configurations with technical rationales, end-to-end traffic flow diagrams, and exact remediation steps.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Centreon Map Integration & Reverse Proxy Chain Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThis report documents the diagnostic findings, configuration changes, and operational status of the Centreon Map reverse proxy chain linking **Centreon Web** (`extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:443`), **Nginx Reverse Proxy** (`th2-revproxyp-fe1`), and **Centreon Map Server** (`172.30.198.50:9443`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key Findings & Root Cause Analysis\n\n### A. Initial 502 Bad Gateway on Port 9443\n* **Observation**: Requests to `https://<reverse-proxy>:9443/` returned `502 Bad Gateway`.\n* **Root Cause**: The original Nginx configuration defined `proxy_pass http://172.30.198.50;` (plain HTTP port 80). Port 80 on `172.30.198.50` was completely closed (`Connection refused`). Centreon Map is powered by Apache Tomcat listening strictly on **HTTPS port 9443** with TLS.\n\n### B. Firewall Hairpin NAT Absence\n* **Observation**: Backend `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49`) could not reach public IP `109.62.64.18:9443`.\n* **Root Cause**: Synchronized packet captures on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` showed `0 packets` arriving when requests were directed to `109.62.64.18`. The perimeter firewall gateway (`172.30.198.54`) performs Destination NAT (DNAT) exclusively for incoming WAN traffic. It does not perform NAT loopback / Hairpin NAT for internal DMZ traffic targeting its own public VIP.\n\n### C. Subnet Separation & Routing Constraints\n* **Observation**: Attempting `ip route add 109.62.64.18/32 via 172.30.198.33` on `th2-centprop-be1` failed with `Error: Nexthop has invalid gateway`.\n* **Root Cause**: Central (`172.30.198.49`) is on subnet `172.30.198.48/29` while the reverse proxy (`172.30.198.33`) is on `172.30.198.32/29`. A host cannot use an IP outside its own broadcast subnet as a direct next-hop gateway without layer-3 routing via `.54`.\n\n### D. UI \"Test Connection to Server\" Button Failure\n* **Observation**: In Centreon Web (`Administration > Extensions > Options`), the \"Test connection to server\" button failed, while CLI `curl -k` succeeded with `HTTP/2 401 Unauthorized` (the expected Centreon Map unauthenticated response).\n* **Root Cause**: Centreon Web PHP initiates a cURL request with strict SSL peer verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = true`). The SSL certificate currently deployed on Nginx port 9443 (`/etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem`) was issued solely with CN/SAN `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`. It lacks `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`. Consequently, PHP cURL rejects the TLS handshake due to hostname mismatch.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Applied Configurations & Technical Rationale\n\n### A. Reverse Proxy: [`th2-revproxyp-fe1`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) (`172.30.198.33`)\n\n#### 1. Nginx Port 9443 Server Block\nConfigured in [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 9443 ssl http2 reuseport;\n    server_name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr 109.62.64.18;\n\n    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/privkey.pem;\n    ssl_trusted_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/chain.pem;\n\n    # Redirect root to Map application context\n    location = / {\n        return 301 /centreon-map/;\n    }\n\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n        proxy_ssl_verify off;\n\n        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;\n\n        # WebSocket support for live Map monitoring streams\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n* **Rationale**:\n  * `proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;`: Directs traffic to Tomcat's actual HTTPS port and accepts Tomcat's internal certificate without validation failures.\n  * `location = / { return 301 /centreon-map/; }`: Prevents Tomcat's default 404 response on `/` by redirecting to the active Centreon Map servlet.\n  * `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;` & `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;`: Guarantees that internal redirects generated by Tomcat preserve port `9443` rather than dropping to standard port `443`.\n  * `Upgrade` and `Connection` headers: Ensures full compatibility with Centreon Map real-time WebSocket notifications.\n\n#### 2. Loopback VIP Interface\nConfigured in [`/etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias`](file:///etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias):\n\n```text\nauto lo:1\niface lo:1 inet static\n    address 109.62.64.18/32\n```\n* **Rationale**: Binds the public VIP `109.62.64.18` directly to loopback on the reverse proxy. Any packet addressed to this IP reaching `th2-revproxyp-fe1` is accepted locally by the Linux network stack and processed by Nginx.\n\n---\n\n### B. Centreon Central Backend: [`th2-centprop-be1`](file:///etc/hosts) (`172.30.198.49`)\n\nAdded to [`/etc/hosts`](file:///etc/hosts):\n\n```text\n172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n```\n\n* **Rationale**:\n  * Directly routes backend-to-reverse-proxy requests over the internal network (`172.30.198.33`).\n  * Completely bypasses the missing hairpin NAT on firewall `172.30.198.54`.\n  * Preserves the official hostname `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` in HTTP Host headers for correct vhost matching and SSL handshakes.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Current Status of the Communication Chain\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph External_Users[\"External Clients\"]\n        ExtBrowser[\"Client Web Browser\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Perimeter[\"Network Boundary\"]\n        FW[\"Firewall Gateway\\n172.30.198.54\\n(WAN DNAT: 109.62.64.18:9443 -> .33)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph DMZ[\"DMZ Subnet 172.30.198.32/29\"]\n        RevProxy[\"th2-revproxyp-fe1\\n172.30.198.33\\n(Nginx: 443 & 9443)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph LAN_Backend[\"Central Subnet 172.30.198.48/29\"]\n        CentralBE[\"th2-centprop-be1\\n172.30.198.49\\n(Centreon Web UI & PHP)\"]\n        CentreonMap[\"Centreon Map Server\\n172.30.198.50:9443\\n(Apache Tomcat)\"]\n    end\n\n    ExtBrowser -->|\"HTTPS :443 (Web UI)\"| FW\n    ExtBrowser -->|\"HTTPS :9443 (Map UI)\"| FW\n    FW -->|\"Port 443 DNAT\"| RevProxy\n    FW -->|\"Port 9443 DNAT\"| RevProxy\n\n    RevProxy -->|\"proxy_pass :80\"| CentralBE\n    RevProxy -->|\"proxy_pass :9443 (TLS)\"| CentreonMap\n\n    CentralBE -.->|\"/etc/hosts direct routing\\n(Fails: SAN mismatch in PHP cURL)\"| RevProxy\n```\n\n| Component / Path | Status | Verification Detail |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **Reverse Proxy Nginx** | **ONLINE** | `nginx -t` passed, syntax clean, listening on `:443` and `:9443` |\n| **Reverse Proxy $\\rightarrow$ Map (`.50:9443`)** | **ONLINE** | `curl -k https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/` returns `401 Unauthorized` |\n| **External WAN $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy** | **READY** | Firewall DNAT forwards `109.62.64.18:9443` $\\rightarrow$ `172.30.198.33:9443` |\n| **Central $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy (Network)** | **ONLINE** | TCP connectivity to `172.30.198.33:9443` verified; `curl -k` succeeds |\n| **Centreon Web UI Connection Test** | **BLOCKED (SSL)** | PHP cURL validates certificate SAN; cert only has `extranetclient...` |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Final Action Required to Complete Validation\n\nTo make the **\"Test connection to server\"** button in Centreon Web turn green:\n\n1. **Expand Certificate SAN on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`**:\n   Add `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the existing Let's Encrypt certificate:\n   ```bash\n   sudo certbot certonly --cert-name extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr \\\n     --expand -d extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr,map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n   ```\n   *(Or run the team's automated DNS-01 playbook `~/.ansible/playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml`).*\n\n2. **Reload Nginx**:\n   ```bash\n   sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx\n   ```\n\n3. **Retest Centreon UI**:\n   In Centreon Web (`Administration > Extensions > Options`), click **\"Test connection to server\"**. With the valid SAN, PHP cURL will validate the certificate chain and report successful connectivity.\n","Description":"Generated comprehensive findings and status report artifact for the Centreon Map reverse proxy chain integration.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md","toolAction":"Creating report artifact","toolSummary":"Centreon Map Chain Report"}}]}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000006.jsonl:4:{"step_index":440,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:53:04Z","content":"A comprehensive technical report has been compiled and saved to the artifact:\n👉 [centreon-map-chain-report.md](file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md)\n\n---\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\n1. **Root Cause of the UI Test Failure**:\n   * Network, routing, and HTTP reverse proxy layers are **fully operational** (CLI `curl -k` receives `401 Unauthorized` directly from Centreon Map's Tomcat engine).\n   * The Centreon Web UI button (*\"Test connection to server\"*) fails because its internal PHP cURL function enforces strict SSL hostname verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = true`). The certificate currently served on port `9443` only covers `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` and lacks `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` as a Subject Alternative Name (SAN).\n\n2. **Configurations Applied & Why**:\n   * **[`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)** (`172.30.198.33`):\n     * Switched upstream to `https://172.30.198.50:9443;` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;` (resolves initial 502 Bad Gateway).\n     * Added root redirect `/` $\\rightarrow$ `/centreon-map/` (prevents Tomcat 404s).\n     * Preserved headers (`Host $http_host;`, `X-Forwarded-Port 9443;`) so internal Tomcat redirects retain port `9443`.\n   * **[`/etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias`](file:///etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias)** (`172.30.198.33`):\n     * Bound `109.62.64.18/32` to loopback (`lo:1`) to ensure local packet acceptance for the VIP.\n   * **[`/etc/hosts`](file:///etc/hosts)** (`172.30.198.49`):\n     * Added `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to route internal backend requests directly to the reverse proxy, bypassing the lack of firewall Hairpin NAT.\n\n---\n\n### Single Action Needed to Complete Validation\n\nExpand the Let's Encrypt certificate on [`th2-revproxyp-fe1`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) to include the `map.*` SAN:\n\n```bash\nsudo certbot certonly --cert-name extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr \\\n  --expand -d extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr,map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\nsudo systemctl reload nginx\n```\n\nOnce reloaded, re-running the test button in Centreon Web will validate with a green success status."}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000006.jsonl:8:{"step_index":444,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:59:43Z","content":"Using a **dedicated Nginx configuration file** and a **dedicated TLS certificate** for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` is not only completely valid, but **architecturally cleaner and best-practice** for enterprise environments.\n\n---\n\n### Key Advantages of This Approach\n\n1. **Separation of Concerns (Modularity)**:\n   * [`02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) handles strictly **Centreon Web** (`:443`) and LoRaWAN (`:8443`).\n   * A new [`03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) handles strictly **Centreon Map** (`:9443`).\n   * Modifications, restarts, or maintenance on Map will never impact Centreon Web availability.\n\n2. **Independent Certificate Lifecycles**:\n   * If one domain encounters an ACME renewal issue (e.g. temporary DNS glitch or challenge timeout), the other certificate continues renewing independently without risk to the primary portal.\n\n3. **Isolated Logging & Tuning**:\n   * Centreon Map uses high-frequency API calls and long-lived WebSocket connections. A dedicated vhost allows isolated logs:\n     * `/var/log/nginx/centreon-map_access.log`\n     * `/var/log/nginx/centreon-map_error.log`\n   * Timeouts (`proxy_read_timeout 3600s;` for WebSockets) and ModSecurity exclusions can be tuned specifically for Map without weakening Centreon Web's security profile.\n\n---\n\n### What Implementation Looks Like\n\n#### 1. Issue the Dedicated Certificate\nRun Certbot for the subdomain only:\n```bash\nsudo certbot certonly --cert-name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr \\\n  -d map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n```\n*(Files created in `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/`)*\n\n#### 2. Create the Dedicated Vhost\nCreate [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 9443 ssl http2 reuseport;\n    server_name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr 109.62.64.18;\n\n    # Dedicated SSL Certificate\n    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/privkey.pem;\n    ssl_trusted_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/chain.pem;\n\n    # Dedicated Logs\n    access_log /var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient_access.log combined;\n    error_log  /var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient_error.log warn;\n\n    # Root redirect to Map app\n    location = / {\n        return 301 /centreon-map/;\n    }\n\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n        proxy_ssl_verify off;\n\n        proxy_set_header Host $http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;\n\n        # WebSocket support\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;\n        proxy_read_timeout 3600s;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Clean up [`02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)\n* Remove the `server { listen 9443 ... }` block from `02-extranetclient...conf` so port `9443` is exclusively managed by the new file.\n\n#### 4. Enable & Reload\n```bash\nsudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/\nsudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx\n```\n\n---\n\n### Comparison Summary\n\n| Metric | Multi-Domain SAN (Single Cert & File) | Separate Cert & Dedicated File (Recommended) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Effort** | Fast (1 command, no new files) | A few extra minutes to create file & symlink |\n| **Modularity** | Centreon Web and Map tightly coupled | **Fully decoupled & clean** |\n| **Maintenance** | Re-expanding if subdomains change | **Independent per-service lifecycle** |\n| **Troubleshooting** | Shared access/error logs | **Dedicated Map access & error logs** |","thinking":"**Evaluating Separate Proxy Configuration**\n\nConsidering using a dedicated Nginx configuration for the specific subdomain. This would enable applying a distinct TLS certificate specifically for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`. The separation allows for tailored directives and security settings, preventing potential conflicts with the main reverse proxy setup. Verify that the correct Certbot command is employed to generate this specific certificate.\n\n\n**Analyzing Proposed Nginx Configuration**\n\nThe proposed setup offers modularity with dedicated configuration files for different services, such as Centreon Web and Map. Independent certificate management is also a significant advantage, isolating certificate renewals and preventing disruptions. Separating access control and logging will provide enhanced security and easier troubleshooting.\n\nThis approach ensures service independence, simplifying maintenance and reducing the risk of a single component's failure affecting the entire system. Considering these aspects, the proposed architecture offers improved robustness and maintainability.\n\n\n"}
