*Security Headers**: Managed centrally through `nginxconfig.io/security.conf`.\n\n---\n\n### Key Observations & Recommendations\n\n1. **Clean up `ssl_trusted_certificate` mismatch**:\n   * Currently, line 8 and line 73 of `02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` reference `DigiCertCA.crt`. Since the certificate was switched to Certbot/Let's Encrypt, this should either point to the Let's Encrypt chain (`/etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/chain.pem`) or be commented out to eliminate the OCSP warning.\n2. **Upstream Keepalive**:\n   * The proxy configurations for `172.30.198.49` and `172.30.198.50` directly target raw IPs rather than named `upstream` blocks with `keepalive` pools. Defining upstream blocks with persistent HTTP/1.1 keepalive connections would reduce TCP handshake overhead to the Centreon backends.","thinking":"**Assessing Nginx Configuration & Status**\n\nDiagnostic output reveals an active Nginx instance (`nginx/1.18.0`) on the target host (`th2-revproxyp-fe1`). The presence of `ModSecurity-nginx v1.0.3` with 908 rules indicates a web application firewall is running. Systemd reports the service as active since July 2026. A warning regarding SSL stapling, potentially indicating a minor configuration issue, needs further investigation but is likely not critical to core functionality.\n\n\n"}
